Why this NOTICE exists
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The MIT license that covered the upstream code grants the right to
sublicense — meaning derivative works MAY adopt a different (typically
more restrictive) license. Joyglide is GPL-3.0-or-later from its
v0.1.0 public release because the maintainer wants to ensure that
future forks and derived works remain free and accessible to everyone.

The original moutella code remains available under MIT in its own
repository. Any code in this repository that traces back to that
upstream IS still MIT-licensed at its origin point; only the combined
work distributed here is governed by the GPL-3.0-or-later terms.

